{"w":2400,"h":3170,"lines":[{"t":"Audioscripts","h":0.016591466187678705,"y":0.047663569217478496,"w":0.11530662536621093,"x":0.097816936733837137,"c":1},{"w":0.7082533772786459,"y":0.094321766682603725,"t":"The first concert will include music by Liza Lim, who was born in Perth, Western Australia, in","x":0.099808052308284989,"h":0.01324921135646695,"c":1},{"t":"1966. As a child, Lim originally learned to play the piano - like so many children - and also","w":0.69879526774088541,"x":0.097826261414490343,"y":0.10940686967573199,"c":1,"h":0.017501987493376614},{"y":0.12645348866136641,"c":1,"w":0.70825337727864579,"x":0.097888666502751964,"t":"the violin, but when she was 11 her teachers encouraged her to start composing. She tound","h":0.013081394761142673},{"x":0.099741067685710241,"t":"this was her real strength, and she studied and later taught composition, both in Australia and","y":0.1416532868918845,"w":0.71800476074218755,"h":0.016127410070377213,"c":1},{"t":"in other countries. As a composer, she has received commissions from numerous orchestras,","y":0.15835962143273963,"x":0.099808081721052225,"w":0.71976964314778646,"c":1,"h":0.014605494478147518},{"w":0.38797197977701825,"y":0.17308281590587016,"c":1,"x":0.09966240465368334,"h":0.016338016257301247,"t":"other performers and festivals in several countries"},{"w":0.675623779296875,"t":"Liza Lim's compositions are vibrant and full of energy, and she often explores Asian and","h":0.01324921135646695,"y":0.19905362777189228,"c":1,"x":0.099808071893423098},{"x":0.097888667858064105,"w":0.69097890218098956,"c":1,"y":0.21511627919268639,"t":"Australian Aboriginal cultural sources, including the native instrument, the didgeridoo: this","h":0.014536717411847588},{"w":0.68330134073893234,"h":0.013081394761142673,"t":"is featured in a work called The Compass. Her music is very expressive, so although it is","x":0.099808062782325249,"y":0.23110465145391268,"c":1},{"x":0.099808070113065153,"w":0.59692896525065109,"h":0.013249211356466839,"t":"complex, it has the power of connecting with audiences and performers alike.","y":0.24700315433283171,"c":1},{"y":0.26855730162856362,"t":"In the festival we're going to give a semi-staged performance of The Oresteia. This is an","x":0.095896878173519537,"w":0.6834633382161458,"h":0.018730348893896576,"c":1},{"t":"opera in seven parts, based on the trilogy of ancient Greek tragedies by Aeschylus. Lim","h":0.016062202814625559,"c":1,"w":0.6757375081380208,"y":0.28592683585720624,"x":0.099748912981113644},{"t":"composed this when she was in her mid-20s, and she also wrote the text, along with Barrie","y":0.30213516046402689,"x":0.097843174418167395,"h":0.0177825735194449,"w":0.70259933471679692,"c":1},{"y":0.31976744198435825,"t":"Kosky. It's performed by six singers, a dancer, and an orchestra that, as well as standard","x":0.097888668303849902,"w":0.68522074381510412,"c":1,"h":0.014617416309633424},{"y":0.33430232575516838,"t":"orchestral instruments, includes electric guitar, and a traditional Turkish stringed instrument.","w":0.71017272949218746,"h":0.017441859681523564,"x":0.09788867887194859,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Lim wrote that because the stories in the tragedies are not easy to tell, the sounds she","x":0.099808064240648003,"y":0.35173501602204804,"h":0.013090565076761873,"w":0.666026865641276},{"w":0.7141248575846354,"t":"creates are also disturbing, and they include breathing, sobbing, laughing and whistling. The","x":0.097832967053143233,"h":0.01800880853309994,"y":0.36618553722748892,"c":1},{"y":0.38359621442499636,"c":1,"x":0.097888666841962971,"t":"work lasts around 75 minutes, and the rest of the concert will consist of orchestral works by","w":0.70249521891276046,"h":0.014659599400469125},{"w":0.5355086263020834,"c":1,"h":0.014559643501738995,"t":"the British composers Ralph Vaughan Williams and Frederick Delius.","x":0.097888680995983274,"y":0.39968454241593099},{"h":0.011627907256598791,"t":"Q31","y":0.12645348819796598,"x":0.82917466426732567,"w":0.034548943837483637,"c":1},{"x":0.82917466357515113,"t":"Q32","y":0.19767441885761905,"w":0.036468331019083755,"h":0.013081394761142673,"c":1},{"y":0.24563953513668879,"t":"Q33","w":0.036468331019083755,"h":0.013081394761142673,"c":1,"x":0.82917466357515113},{"w":0.66602686564127611,"y":0.44763406958043594,"t":"Moving on now to our second concert, this will begin with instrumental music by British","h":0.014575232617110467,"x":0.099808064204036664,"c":1},{"x":0.097888676469312944,"y":0.46366279082107675,"w":0.68905949910481767,"c":1,"h":0.014570647760144495,"t":"composers - Benjamin Britten and Judith Weir. After the interval we il go to Australia for a"},{"x":0.097888667335582422,"y":0.47949526798233533,"c":1,"w":0.69673706054687501,"h":0.016144266940817831,"t":"piece by Ross Edwards: The Tower of Remoteness. According to Edwards, the inspiration"},{"c":1,"y":0.49558359597424118,"w":0.65067179361979166,"t":"for this piece came from nature, when he was sitting alone in the dry bed of a creek,","h":0.016088328075709812,"x":0.097888671230893898},{"x":0.097888675527796357,"h":0.014555058043085878,"w":0.70057581583658857,"c":1,"t":"overshadowed by the leaves of palm trees, listening to the birds and insects. The Tower of","y":0.51162790709967565},{"w":0.76583491007486981,"h":0.014655013941816009,"c":1,"x":0.099808072697932182,"t":"Remoteness is scored for piano and clarinet. Edwards says he realised years after writing the Q36","y":0.52761627919386678},{"h":0.017090554944348302,"t":"piece that he had subconsciously modelled its opening phrase on a bird call.","y":0.54357545212279479,"w":0.58933975219726564,"x":0.097843609886871033,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.56612664826186332,"w":0.61821253458658854,"x":0.099721775346349517,"h":0.017805118741297199,"t":"Ross Edwards was born in 1943 in Sydney, Australia, and studied at the Sydney"},{"w":0.68522074381510412,"c":1,"x":0.10172743990910381,"t":"Conservatorium of Music and the universities of Adelaide and Sydney. He's well known in","h":0.014627503596645774,"y":0.58284883733229464},{"w":0.68530853271484371,"c":1,"y":0.59800012523596946,"h":0.017009396959178469,"x":0.097843420179085858,"t":"Australia, and in fact he's one of the country's most performed composers. He's written a"},{"x":0.09980807358019092,"t":"wide range of music, from symphonies and concertos to some composed specifically for","h":0.014534883469061177,"y":0.61482558146937305,"w":0.68138193766276034,"c":1},{"h":0.015988372176979682,"c":1,"x":0.097888683148444969,"t":"children. Edwards's music has been described as being 'deeply connected to Australia', and","y":0.63081395344382341,"w":0.71017272949218746},{"h":0.013081394761142673,"c":1,"x":0.097888683142060326,"t":"it can be regarded as a celebration of the diversity of cultures that Australia can be proud of.","y":0.64825581424555845,"w":0.71017272949218746},{"t":"The last of the three Australian composers to be represented in our festival is Carl Vine. Born","x":0.10172743745015547,"c":1,"y":0.67151162819846266,"h":0.013081394761142673,"w":0.71401153564453124},{"y":0.68738170357866268,"t":"in 1954, Vine, like Liza Lim, comes from Perth, Western Australia. He took up the cornet at","w":0.70057581583658857,"x":0.097888674745539014,"h":0.014653179999029597,"c":1},{"h":0.016732916847012391,"c":1,"t":"the age of five, switching to the piano five years later. However, he went to university to study","x":0.097834285090839135,"y":0.70329667011495456,"w":0.71795761108398437},{"c":1,"t":"physics, before changing to composition. After graduating he moved to Sydney and worked","x":0.099763819053650407,"h":0.015399536349419929,"w":0.70257588704427087,"y":0.71925139230711088},{"y":0.73690851705431026,"t":"as a treelance planist and composer. Before long he had become prominent in Australia as a","x":0.099808060297552667,"w":0.71209213256835946,"c":1,"h":0.013091482649842279},{"h":0.016332030672380204,"t":"composer for dance. and in fact has written 25 scores of that type.","y":0.74968755633320072,"x":0.099740031763849019,"w":0.51263468424479164,"c":1},{"y":0.77470930244876302,"t":"In our third concert, Vine will be represented by his music for the flag hand-over ceremony","x":0.099808070368240659,"w":0.69289825439453123,"h":0.014565145330098117,"c":1},{"h":0.017788426733167384,"x":0.09782018895191584,"w":0.68728668212890631,"t":"of the Olympics held in 1996. This seven-minute orchestral piece was of course heard by","y":0.78892800176346367,"c":1},{"h":0.01162790725659868,"c":1,"t":"Q40","x":0.82917466357448466,"y":0.79215116261847063,"w":0.036468331019083644},{"y":0.80662460593908314,"w":0.70057581583658857,"h":0.014596324162528318,"t":"millions of people worldwide, and we'll hear it alongside works written by British composers","x":0.099808061140544829,"c":1},{"w":0.37619962056477874,"c":1,"y":0.82267441872643299,"h":0.014549556214726644,"t":"Edward Elgar and, more recently, Thomas Adès.","x":0.099808059092987705},{"h":0.013081394761142673,"x":0.097888675085467766,"y":0.95203488397630265,"c":1,"w":0.036468331019083658,"t":"112"}]}